WEBVTT

1
00:00:00.800 --> 00:00:02.584
You've made the explainer video.

2
00:00:02.634 --> 00:00:04.036
Now where does it go?

3
00:00:04.086 --> 00:00:08.577
In the wrong spot it's decoration; in the right spot, it works every day.

4
00:00:09.077 --> 00:00:11.651
Every explainer answers one question.

5
00:00:11.701 --> 00:00:15.203
Write it down, then ask where a visitor is when they have it.

6
00:00:15.253 --> 00:00:17.086
That's where the video goes.

7
00:00:18.336 --> 00:00:26.252
Put home and pricing videos high on the page, walkthroughs beside the feature description, and help videos at the top of the matching article.

8
00:00:27.502 --> 00:00:29.844
You don't need five separate productions.

9
00:00:29.894 --> 00:00:35.662
Duplicate one master deck, cut it down for each page, and adjust the speaker notes for the audience.

10
00:00:36.912 --> 00:00:39.753
Small details decide who presses play.

11
00:00:39.803 --> 00:00:46.536
Tell people what they'll get and how long it takes, lead with a clear headline, and add captions for sound-off browsing.

12
00:00:47.786 --> 00:00:52.868
When the product changes, edit the slides and export again, no reshoot.

13
00:00:52.918 --> 00:00:55.654
On Pro, a.i. directs each video.

14
00:00:55.704 --> 00:00:58.267
Try Basic first, with no subscription.

15
00:00:58.317 --> 00:01:00.916
Start at powerpoint2vid.com.

